course: dictionary
lesson: 15435
title: A word like a statue
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Statuesque describes someone who is tall, graceful and impressive, the way a statue looks. You will mostly meet it in stories and descriptions. «The statuesque queen stood at the top of the stairs, tall and calm.»
explain: Look for the clues around the word. Tall, graceful, stood and calm all point to a grand, elegant figure. Try your meaning in the sentence: "The tall, graceful queen stood at the top of the stairs" still makes sense, so you are on the right track.
explain: The word can also mean very still, like a statue. «The heron stood statuesque in the shallow water, waiting for a fish.» The heron is not just tall. It is so still that it looks like a statue.
explain: Statuesque is a formal or literary word. Writers use it to praise someone's height, poise and calm, so you will often see it in descriptions of athletes, models or queens.
fact: Statuesque means tall, graceful and impressive, like a statue.
fact: Statuesque can also mean very still, like a statue.
fact: It is usually used to describe a person, often a woman.
fact: It is a formal or literary word, found in stories, descriptions and writing about athletes or models.
fact: The word comes from statue, and -esque means in the style of, so statuesque means in the style of a statue.
exercise: «The statuesque dancer raised one arm and held perfectly still.» What does statuesque suggest here? | *Tall, graceful and still, like a statue | Loud and messy | Very small and quick | Sleepy and tired
exercise: Maya says statuesque means messy. What does it really mean? | Untidy and crumpled | Wet and muddy | Quiet and nervous | *Tall, graceful and impressive
exercise: «The statuesque guard did not move once all night.» What does statuesque tell you about the guard? | Very cross and loud | *Very still, like a statue | Very hungry | Very fast on his feet
test: «The statuesque model walked onto the stage, tall and calm.» What does statuesque mean? | Dirty and tired | Loud and noisy | *Tall, graceful and impressive | Small and nervous
test: «The statuesque athlete waited at the start line, not moving a muscle.» Which clue shows that statuesque means still? | The start line | Athlete | Waited | *Not moving a muscle
exam: Which best describes a statuesque queen? | Small and giggly | Wet and grey | *Tall, graceful and still, like a statue | Loud and rushed
